          %h4#AsProperEtaleGroupoidDuggerCofibrant Dugger-cofibrant model
          %p
            For computing
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+functors"} derived functors
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mapping+stacks"} mapping stacks
            out of a spindle orbifold, it is useful to have a
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves#DuggerSufficientProjectiveCofibrancyCondition"} Dugger cofibrant model
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+nerve"} simplicial nerve
            is in each degree
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeomorphism"} diffeomorphic
            to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disjoint+union"} disjoint union
            of
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+spaces"} Cartesian spaces
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+balls"} open balls
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/degeneracy+maps"} degeneracy maps
            are inclusions of disjoint summands.
          %p We describe this in pictures, which should make the actual definition obvious.
          %p
            First consider the Dugger-cofibrant resolution of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+groupoid"} action groupoid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi 𝔻
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                      %mo +
                      %mi ϵ
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ⫽
                  %msub
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{D}^2_{1+ \epsilon} \sslash \mathbb{Z}_n
            which is obtained from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+good+open+cover"} equivariant good open cover
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi 𝔻
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                      %mo +
                      %mi ϵ
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{D}^2_{1+\epsilon}
            whose charts are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tubular+neighbourhoods"} tubular neighbourhoods
            of the
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            sectors where the evident
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/angle"} angle
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coordinate"} coordinate
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi α
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝔻
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ∖
                  %msub
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mo ≥
                      %mn 0
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha \colon \mathbb{D}^2 \setminus \mathbb{R}_{\geq 0} \longrightarrow \mathbb{R}
            is within
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                      %mfrac
                        %mrow
                          %mi k
                          %mo +
                          %mn 1
                        %mi n
                    %mo ≥
                    %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                      %mfrac
                        %mi α
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mn 2
                          %mi π
                    %mo ≥
                    %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                      %mfrac
                        %mi k
                        %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tfrac{k+1}{n} \geq  \tfrac{\alpha}{n 2 \pi } \geq \tfrac{k}{n}
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo ∈
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo ,
                    %mi n
                    %mo −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k \in \{0, 1, \cdots, n-1\}
          %p
            This is illustrated in the following graphic for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo =
                  %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 3
            (cf. the non-equivariant version
            %a{:href => "#Čech+groupoid#Idea"} here
            at
            = succeed ")." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C4%8Cech+groupoid"} Čech groupoid
          %div{:style => "margin: -30px 0px 20px 30px"}
            %img{:src => "/nlab/files/EquivariantChechGroupoidIllustration-251101.png", :width => "700px"}/
          %p
            We want to glue two such equivariant Čech groupoids by gluing the
            = succeed "-collars" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϵ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \epsilon
            = succeed "-case)" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 3
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (2,3)
          %div{:style => "margin: -30px 0px 20px 30px"}
            %img{:src => "/nlab/files/SpindleGluingMorphismIllustration-251101.png", :width => "700px"}/
          %p To note here that the composition of any two of these gluing morphisms is translation by one of the two group actions, hence may be identified with a morphism in one of the two action groupoids.
          %p
            In total, the resulting Lie groupoid presentation of the spindle looks as indicated in the following graphics for
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi n
                      %mo +
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 3
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n_+, n_-) = (2,3)
          %div{:style => "margin: -30px 0px 20px 30px"}
            %img{:src => "/nlab/files/DuggerCofibrantSpindleGroupoid-251101.png", :width => "700px"}/
